column5:
This looks like the perfect place to rest.{w}
I have a seat, and try taking in everything I can.{w}
In such a short period of time, everything changed.{w}
I hope that we're able to set things right.

column6:
这里看起来是绝佳的歇脚之处。{w}
我坐下来，尽量把眼前的一切都收入眼底。{w}
如此短暂的时间里，一切都变了。{w}
但愿我们能让一切重回正轨。

column5:
This isn't a spirit idol, but it looks similar to one.{w}
Perhaps the energy present caused a small one to grow.{w}
It seems to defy physics, floating and rotating.{w}
The perpetual motion is actually entrancing.

column6:
这不是灵像，但外形与之相似。{w}
也许是此处的灵力催生出了一个小小的灵像。{w}
它悬浮旋转，仿佛不受物理法则约束。{w}
这种永恒的运动，竟令人着迷。

column5:
This is it. This is where I grabbed The Blade of Exodus.{w}
Where I saw those visions, and the future to come.{w}
As a Seer of Valinorth, only I could wield it.{w}
I was to be the instrument of Alestia's liberation.

column6:
就是这里。我就是在这里握住了流亡之刃。{w}
在这里，我看到了那些幻象，以及即将到来的未来。{w}
身为瓦利诺斯的先知，只有我能执掌它。{w}
我注定要成为解放阿莱斯提亚的利器。

column5:
He knocked on the hard wall of the cell, and found nothing.{w}
He'd been here ever since Damek assumed control of The Rebellion.{w}
His objective was to get caught on purpose, and scan their castle.{w}
But his intel would do little good if this was his final resting place.

column6:
他敲了敲牢房坚硬的墙壁，一无所获。{w}
自达梅克接管反抗军以来，他就一直被关在这里。{w}
他的任务就是故意被捕，再探查他们的城堡。{w}
可要是这里成了他的葬身之地，那情报就毫无意义了。

column5:
Shane felt a sense of hope rise within him.{w}
If Sovy tried to recruit him, he could gain more intel.{w}
It wouldn't be hard to miss his shots on purpose.{w}
Unfortunately, his hopes were immediately destroyed.

column6:
肖恩心中升起一丝希望。{w}
若是索维想招募他，他就能套取更多情报。{w}
故意射偏几箭也不难。{w}
可惜，他的希望转瞬破灭。

column5:
I look off the side of the bridge, and shiver.{w}
It's higher than you'd think, that's for sure.{w}
The grass is almost as tall as a fully grown man.{w}
Falling down there? Now {i}that{/i} would be scary.

column6:
我朝桥边望去，不禁打了个寒颤。{w}
这桥比你想的要高得多，这是肯定的。{w}
下面的草几乎有成年人那么高。{w}
摔下去？那{i}才{/i}叫可怕。

column5:
The trees go on forever, but they are all small in comparison.{w}
The Grand Tree looms above all else, and it's incredible.{w}
I can't see how far back they go, but some sun rays shine through.{w}
From here, it looks as if all of Alestia is one large forest.

column6:
树林绵延无尽，但相比之下都显得矮小。{w}
巨树高耸于万物之上，令人叹为观止。{w}
我看不清它们延伸到多远，但有几缕阳光透了下来。{w}
从这里望去，整个阿莱斯提亚仿佛就是一片巨大的森林。

column5:
These posts guide you to The Grand Tree's entrance.{w}
There isn't much upkeep given to the grass on the sides.{w}
If you jumped off, you'd be fully submerged in grass.{w}
It might not look like it, but this is a high bridge.

column6:
这些立柱指引着通往巨树入口的路。{w}
两侧的杂草没怎么打理。{w}
要是跳下去，你会整个陷进草里。{w}
也许看不太出来，但这是座高桥。

column5:
These posts guide you to The Grand Tree's entrance.{w}
There isn't much upkeep given to the grass on the sides.{w}
If you jumped off, you'd be fully submerged in grass.{w}
It might not look like it, but this is a high bridge.

column6:
这些立柱指引着通往巨树入口的路。{w}
两侧的杂草没怎么打理。{w}
要是跳下去，你会整个陷进草里。{w}
也许看不太出来，但这是座高桥。

column5:
This bridge leads all the way to The Grand Tree.{w}
It's a farther walk than it looks, that's for sure.{w}
Townspeople pitch in to make sure it's always stable.{w}
Wouldn't want the bridge to break halfway across.

column6:
这座桥一直通向巨树。{w}
走起来比看起来远得多，这是肯定的。{w}
镇民们出力维护，确保它始终稳固。{w}
可不想走到半路桥塌了。

column5:
Without a doubt, the most impressive sight in Valinorth.{w}
No one knows just how high The Grand Tree grows.{w}
But the bottom of it is hollow, and easily accessed.{w}
It became a sacred ground for Seers and Scribes to meet.

column6:
毫无疑问，这是瓦利诺斯最令人震撼的景象。{w}
没人知道巨树究竟能长多高。{w}
但它的底部中空，很容易进入。{w}
这里成了先知与书记官会面的圣地。

column5:
You can see the tint of the leaves start to change.{w}
The higher up you go, the more crimson they get.{w}
Bloodleaves grow at the top of The Grand Tree.{w}
No one knows the reason for this phenomenon.

column6:
你能看到叶片的色泽开始变化。{w}
越往上，越是深红。{w}
血叶生长在巨树的顶端。{w}
没人知道这种现象的缘由。

column5:
We nod, and we stand up as well.{w}
With an attack on the way, we had to move.{w}
Mylus would take care of evacuating everyone else.{w}
If we got that blade first, Sovy couldn't use it.

column6:
我们点点头，也站起身来。{w}
袭击将至，我们必须行动。{w}
迈勒斯会负责疏散其他人。{w}
只要我们抢先拿到那把剑，索维就用不了它。

column5:
Mylus isn't using this desk, so I assume it's fair game.{w}
I push aside a few papers, looking for anything of note.{w}
A book on Sauleberg grabs my interest, as he brought it up.{w}
Apparently, the spirit idol there has stopped giving off energy.

column6:
迈勒斯没在用这张桌子，我想翻翻也无妨。{w}
我拨开几张纸，寻找任何值得留意的东西。{w}
一本关于索尔伯格的书引起了我的兴趣，毕竟他刚提起过。{w}
看样子，那里的灵像已经不再释放灵力了。

column5:
I look through all the books, but nothing seems interesting.{w}
Everything that Mylus found worth in was already on the table.{w}
That, and on his little desk by the window facing Valinorth.{w}
Must be great to live in a place with such a nice view.

column6:
我翻遍了所有的书，没什么有意思的。{w}
迈勒斯觉得有价值的东西，都已经摆在桌上了。{w}
还有窗边那张面向瓦利诺斯的小书桌上。{w}
住在风景这么好的地方，一定很棒。

column5:
It's a map of the known world, far on the back of the wall.{w}
We're in Valinorth, with Mazeo a little bit North of us.{w}
To the East of Mazeo is Alarinthia, and further north is Balteus.{w}
I have a feeling we'd be going to Balteus, The Triumvirate's doorstep.

column6:
那是墙最里侧的一张已知世界地图。{w}
我们在瓦利诺斯，马泽奥就在我们北边一点。{w}
马泽奥以东是阿拉林西亚，再往北是巴尔泰乌斯。{w}
我有种预感，我们会去巴尔泰乌斯——三人执政团的家门口。

column5:
The carpeted area is warm, next to a large fireplace.{w}
Only the most expensive homes in Valinorth have these.{w}
Scattered about the carpet are various trinkets and pipes.{w}
I guess an Elder isn't mystical enough without a smoking pipe.

column6:
铺地毯的那一角挨着一座大壁炉，暖意融融。{w}
瓦利诺斯只有最昂贵的宅邸才有这种配置。{w}
地毯上散落着各种小玩意和烟斗。{w}
看来长老少了根烟斗，就不够有神秘感。

column5:
I can see the entire town from here, and it's beautiful.{w}
I take a deep breath and admire the view, one final time.{w}
This might be the last time I see Valinorth fully intact.{w}
When my vision came to pass, only ruin would remain here.

column6:
从这里能看见整个镇子，美极了。{w}
我深吸一口气，最后一次欣赏这景色。{w}
这也许是我最后一次见到完好无损的瓦利诺斯。{w}
当我的幻象成真，这里只会剩下废墟。

column5:
Damek conversed with Gryz, the Mayor of Mazeo.{w}
There was much to be done before The Rebellion could settle down.{w}
But first on his agenda, was procuring the city's undergound tunnels.{w}
A place to operate in secrecy would be essential to their continued success.

column6:
达梅克正与马泽奥市长格瑞兹交谈。{w}
反抗军要安顿下来，还有太多事要做。{w}
但他的当务之急，是获取这座城市的地下隧道。{w}
一个能秘密行动的地方，对他们持续的成功至关重要。

column5:
Sovy stood in front of The Triumvirate's castle.{w}
With Shane at his side, everything was set in motion.{w}
Halin was late, likely learning the same truth from his Masters.{w}
But as soon as he arrived, their plan of attack would commence.

column6:
索维站在三人执政团的城堡前。{w}
肖恩在他身旁，一切已开始运转。{w}
哈林迟到了，多半是从他的主上那里得知了同样的真相。{w}
但他一到，他们的进攻计划就会启动。
